nodecode-grounder is a rewrite of grounder-labs's grounder-labs/grounder-hermes-plugin:

  https://github.com/grounder-labs/grounder-hermes-plugin
  commit 4c0e58799b2f2c2258f143d9e97ea7d3ff37ebeb

Apache-2.0, Copyright (c) 2026 Grounder Labs, Inc. (LICENSE)

That repository's LICENSE is here unchanged; its appendix keeps Apache's placeholder
for the copyright line, and the holder named above is the one its README and NOTICE
write ("Copyright 2026 Grounder Labs, Inc.").

Rewritten: provider.py's one search, as provider.lisp was: the same POST to
https://api.grounder.net/v1/search, the same JSON body (query cut to 2000
characters, top_k clamped to 1-20, text_max_chars at 800), the search key in the
same bearer header, the same user-agent shape, and the same rows out -- a result's
title, its url, and a description that is its summary else its text on one line,
at most 800 characters and marked with an ellipsis when a response ran past the
budget. Its four failure sentences (a refused key, a rate limit, an HTTP status,
a body that is not JSON) are here, with the transport failure it caught too. The
plugin's one contribution -- register() adding the `grounder' web-search provider,
selected with web.search_backend -- is here the grounder_search tool, the same call
as the verb (grounder:search ...) from eval and as /grounder, and the one section
that holds what GROUNDER_API_KEY held and Hermes's own configuration held besides.

Left out: the OAuth sign-in. Hermes stored, refreshed and attached that grant
(`hermes auth add grounder:grounder`), and the plugin kept no credential of its
own; a Nodecode cell has no such grant to be handed, so the search key the same
plugin already accepted is the one way in here, read from the section or from
GROUNDER_API_KEY. Also left out: Hermes's keyless-fallback retry and its own
web_extract, which were Hermes's behaviour around the plugin rather than the
plugin; and the {"success": false, "error": ...} envelope, since a refusal here
is a condition carrying Grounder's own sentence. Nothing else of the plugin is
missing: it had no commands, hooks, skills or prompts beyond the provider.
